---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Voice - wReady Showcase" description="Original poem exploring authenticity and creative expression">
  <article class="poem-detail">
    
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="poem-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/wready">wReady</a> / <a href="/wready/poems">Poems</a> / Voice
        </div>
        <h1>Voice</h1>
        <div class="poem-meta">
          <span class="meta-item"><strong>Form:</strong> Free Verse</span>
          <span class="meta-item"><strong>Status:</strong> Published</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Poem Content -->
    <section class="poem-content">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="poem-text">
          <div class="stanza">
            <p>
              The voice that speaks through silence<br>
              carries weight the shouting never could—<br>
              a whisper in the margins,<br>
              ink bleeding through the page.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="stanza">
            <p>
              We mistake volume for truth,<br>
              confuse the echo with the source,<br>
              but the real work happens<br>
              in the quiet spaces between words.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="stanza">
            <p>
              Listen for what isn't said—<br>
              the pause before the answer,<br>
              the breath held back,<br>
              the sentence left unfinished.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="stanza">
            <p>
              That's where meaning lives,<br>
              where authenticity hides<br>
              from the performance,<br>
              waiting to be found.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="stanza">
            <p>
              Your voice is not the loudest one—<br>
              it's the one that sounds like you<br>
              when no one else is listening,<br>
              when you've forgotten to pretend.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Analysis -->
    <section class="analysis-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>About This Poem</h2>
        
        <div class="analysis-grid">
          <div class="analysis-card">
            <h3>Theme</h3>
            <p>
              An exploration of authenticity and the power of restraint in creative expression. 
              The poem examines how genuine voice emerges not from volume or performance, 
              but from careful attention to the spaces between words.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="analysis-card">
            <h3>Form & Structure</h3>
            <p>
              Free verse with five stanzas of four lines each. The consistent structure 
              creates a meditative rhythm while the lack of rhyme scheme allows the 
              natural voice to emerge without constraint.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="analysis-card">
            <h3>Key Images</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Silence vs. Shouting:</strong> The central contrast between authentic quiet and performative noise</li>
              <li><strong>Margins & Ink:</strong> Writing as a physical, intimate act</li>
              <li><strong>Spaces Between Words:</strong> The importance of what's unsaid</li>
              <li><strong>Listening:</strong> Active engagement rather than passive reception</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="analysis-card">
            <h3>Related Themes</h3>
            <p>
              This poem connects to broader themes of authenticity in creative work, 
              the relationship between artist and audience, and the tension between 
              performance and genuine expression—themes that also appear in the 
              Her Majesty's Displeasure screenplay project.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Technical Features -->
    <section class="technical-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>wReady Poetry Features</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          This poem demonstrates wReady's poetry management capabilities:
        </p>
        
        <div class="features-grid">
          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>📝 Form Analysis</h3>
            <p>Track poetic forms, meter, rhyme schemes, and structural elements</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>🎨 Thematic Connections</h3>
            <p>Link poems to themes and cross-reference with other creative work</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>📊 Collection Organization</h3>
            <p>Group poems into collections with ordering and publication status</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature-item">
            <h3>🔗 Cross-References</h3>
            <p>Connect poems to related songs, themes, and narrative projects</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="cta-box">
          <h2>More Poems</h2>
          <p>Explore other original poetry with form analysis and thematic connections.</p>
          <a href="/wready/poems" class="cta-button">← Back to Poems</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .poem-detail {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .container {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-8);
  }

  /* Hero */
  .poem-hero {
    padding: 3rem 0 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .breadcrumb {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .poem-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .meta-item {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* Poem Content */
  .poem-content {
    padding: 4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .poem-text {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .stanza {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .stanza:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .stanza p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* Analysis */
  .analysis-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }

  .analysis-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .analysis-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .analysis-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .analysis-card p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .analysis-card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .analysis-card li {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .analysis-card strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* Technical Features */
  .technical-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section-intro {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .features-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .feature-item h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .feature-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* CTA */
  .cta-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .cta-box {
    padding: 3rem;
    background: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-box h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .cta-box p {
    margin: 0 0 2rem 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: all var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .cta-button:hover {
    background: var(--accent-dark);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .container {
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    }

    .poem-meta {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .analysis-grid,
    .features-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .cta-box {
      padding: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>